        "node_id": "n_5_e34f26",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The issue lies in the calculation of the expected value. Instead of computing the expected value directly, we should calculate the probability of each possible longest increasing subsequence length and then sum these probabilities multiplied by their respective lengths. This approach will correctly handle the fractional probabilities and avoid floating-point precision issues.",
