        "node_id": "n_6_a81099",
        "thought_text": "The current approach is flawed because it only considers sequences of length 3 and does not generalize to sequences of any length N. The nested loops should iterate over the range of A[i] for each i, and the calculation of total_lis_length should account for all possible sequences. Additionally, the expected value calculation needs to be adjusted to properly account for the total number of sequences and the modulo operation.",
